From: WAM / T-39 (PR-07 §8 item 4)
Subject: [PATCH] video_utils: fall back to PyAV when torchcodec cannot load

WHAT THIS IS. The entire delta between the Isaac-GR00T tree that trained
`runs/apple_pnp_h200_frozen` to checkpoint-5000 in July 2026 and upstream
NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T at commit e5749287857afd97b78f1147166137de29746392
(2026-06-18). One file, this one. `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` are
byte-identical to that commit, so the dependency set is upstream's own.

Established by diffing the unpacked tree against 50 upstream commits and taking
the minimum (2026-08-15). The bundle's own RUNBOOK.md describes it as "Our
Isaac-GR00T fork (has the cache-first HF patches)" -- that description is WRONG
and is corrected here: `GROOT_HF_LOCAL_FIRST` and `GROOT_PATCH_MISTRAL` in
`gr00t/__init__.py` are UPSTREAM code, present verbatim at the base commit. We
did not write them. Nothing outside this file is ours.

WHY IT EXISTS. Upstream commit e5749287 itself "simplifies video decoding to
torchcodec-only, removing ffmpeg/decord/opencv/pyav dispatch paths". Discoverer+
ships no FFmpeg -- no module, no system libavutil -- so `torchcodec` raises on
import and every dataloader worker dies. The patch restores a fallback.

WHY IT MATTERS FOR PR-07 §3. §3 requires the trainer "vendored UNMODIFIED", so
that a failure is attributable to NVIDIA's recipe rather than to our copy of it.
This patch is a deliberate, recorded exception, and it is NOT inert here:

  - It is a pure fallback. `_get_video_decoder_cls` still returns torchcodec's
    `VideoDecoder` whenever that imports; the shim is reached only on the
    ImportError/OSError path. On any machine with a working torchcodec the
    behaviour is bit-identical to upstream.
  - On Discoverer+ torchcodec does NOT import, so on THIS cluster the shim is
    live and decodes every training frame. It is in the data path, not beside
    it, and a T-39 result carries it.
  - It touches no model, no trainer, no loss, no optimiser, no data config and
    no hyperparameter. It is a decoder shim.

Whether that counts as "unmodified" for §3 is a judgement, and it is recorded
here rather than resolved silently. The alternative -- installing FFmpeg into
the venv so upstream torchcodec loads unpatched -- was not attempted and would
be the cleaner answer if it works.

APPLY WITH: patch -p1 < this file, from the vendored tree root.
Verified to apply cleanly against e5749287 (`patch -p1 --dry-run`, 2026-08-15).

